# Review

## Summary

I checked every link once per target, comparing each link's text and sentence with the target's title and opening. Most links match. These include the deployed-system note, the deliberative-learning definition, persistent deployment-time adaptation, episode evidence, the Gödel machine, the PRODIGY and EURISKO ingests, the on-balance and reversibility notes, objective revision, the two Bitter Lesson notes, the harness-evolution ingest, compounding, false-positive acceptance, operative change, and the three companion drafts, whose titles match their link text. The "Where to go next" descriptions of the deliberative-learning definition and the on-balance note match sections that exist in those targets.

Two links set up an expectation that the target does not meet. One presents inspectability as a property of form, although the target qualifies form. The other presents a note on rationale-guided repair as a note on whether written rules drive behavior.

External links were not fetched under this run's reading scope: Sutton's Bitter Lesson essay, the Sequoia interview and the GitHub Discussions page. The KB's Bitter Lesson note cites the same essay URL and an ingest of the same interview, consistent with the link text.
